```
The walrus in the return dict re-computes spread. If `primary` is empty, `spread` is unbound but guarded by `if primary else None` — but Python evaluates the walrus only if the condition is true? Yes, conditional expression evaluates lazily. Fine. If primary non-empty, spread recomputed identically. No bug.

